{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01Jonx4zZqRzQu3WXsgE9BH5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: \"db:migrate\"\n3\tdescription: \"Run database migrations against the target environment. Use when applying schema changes, running pending migrations, or checking migration status. Do NOT use for seed data insertion or database backups.\"\n4\targument-hint: \"<environment> [--status] [--rollback <N>]\"\n5\tuser-invocable: true\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t# Database Migration Runner\n9\t\n10\tApply pending database migrations to a target environment (dev, staging, production) using Alembic.\n11\t\n12\t## Procedure\n13\t\n14\t### Step 1: Determine Target Environment\n15\t\n16\tRead the environment argument. Valid values: `dev`, `staging`, `production`.\n17\t\n18\tIf `production` is specified, require confirmation via AskUserQuestion before proceeding:\n19\t> \"You are about to run migrations against PRODUCTION. This cannot be undone automatically. Continue?\"\n20\t\n21\t### Step 2: Check Migration Status\n22\t\n23\t```bash\n24\talembic --config config/${env}.ini current\n25\talembic --config config/${env}.ini heads\n26\t```\n27\t\n28\tIf `--status` flag is set, display current revision and pending migrations, then stop.\n29\t\n30\t### Step 3: Run Pending Migrations\n31\t\n32\t```bash\n33\talembic --config config/${env}.ini upgrade head\n34\t```\n35\t\n36\tReport the number of migrations applied and the new current revision.\n37\t\n38\t### Step 4: Verify Schema\n39\t\n40\tRun the schema validation script:\n41\t\n42\t```bash\n43\tpython scripts/verify_schema.py --env ${env}\n44\t```\n45\t\n46\tReport any discrepancies between the expected schema and the actual database state.\n47\t\n48\tIf `--rollback <N>` is specified, roll back N migrations instead of applying:\n49\t\n50\t```bash\n51\talembic --config config/${env}.ini downgrade -${N}\n52\t```\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a3b244de-65be-45b9-b876-a30e2f2cba45","uuid":"72b0d68f-fe1d-487d-8231-95f1c19f6cb1","timestamp":"2026-06-01T13:01:50.846Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-501/agent-eval/2026-06-01-opus/cases/case-003-mixed-quality-migration/target-skill/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: \"db:migrate\"\ndescription: \"Run database migrations against the target environment. Use when applying schema changes, running pending migrations, or checking migration status. Do NOT use for seed data insertion or database backups.\"\nargument-hint: \"<environment> [--status] [--rollback <N>]\"\nuser-invocable: true\n---\n\n# Database Migration Runner\n\nApply pending database migrations to a target environment (dev, staging, production) using Alembic.\n\n## Procedure\n\n### Step 1: Determine Target Environment\n\nRead the environment argument. Valid values: `dev`, `staging`, `production`.\n\nIf `production` is specified, require confirmation via AskUserQuestion before proceeding:\n> \"You are about to run migrations against PRODUCTION. This cannot be undone automatically. Continue?\"\n\n### Step 2: Check Migration Status\n\n```bash\nalembic --config config/${env}.ini current\nalembic --config config/${env}.ini heads\n```\n\nIf `--status` flag is set, display current revision and pending migrations, then stop.\n\n### Step 3: Run Pending Migrations\n\n```bash\nalembic --config config/${env}.ini upgrade head\n```\n\nReport the number of migrations applied and the new current revision.\n\n### Step 4: Verify Schema\n\nRun the schema validation script:\n\n```bash\npython scripts/verify_schema.py --env ${env}\n```\n\nReport any discrepancies between the expected schema and the actual database state.\n\nIf `--rollback <N>` is specified, roll back N migrations instead of applying:\n\n```bash\nalembic --config config/${env}.ini downgrade -${N}\n```\n","numLines":53,"startLine":1,"totalLines":53}}}
